\subsection{Qualitative Case Study}
\label{app:case-study}

We present three representative document chains from our depth-generation pipeline, illustrating how text properties evolve across generation depths 0--3.
Depth~0 is the original human-written text; each subsequent depth is produced by prompting the generator (Qwen-1.5B) with the text from the preceding depth.
For each case, we report three key features from our 15-dimensional OBD feature set: type-token ratio (TTR), mean surprisal, and frequency entropy.

\paragraph{Case A: C4 Web Content (Stylistic Convergence).}
A vacation rental listing (depth~0) with fragmented promotional phrases converges to generic real-estate prose by depth~1. Depths~2 and~3 produce near-identical property descriptions, illustrating feature saturation consistent with $K^*{=}2$.

\begin{center}
{\footnotesize
\begin{tabular}{lcccc}
\toprule
& \textbf{Depth 0} & \textbf{Depth 1} & \textbf{Depth 2} & \textbf{Depth 3} \\
\midrule
TTR & 0.683 & 0.659 & 0.628 & 0.604 \\
Mean Surprisal & \textbf{3.434} & 2.098 & 2.091 & 2.155 \\
Freq.\ Entropy & \textbf{5.767} & 6.599 & 6.631 & 6.682 \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}}
\end{center}

\noindent\textsc{Depth~0 (human):} {\small\itshape Cs By the Sea - Walk Out Straight to the Beach in Seagrove 30A! The Sandlot... Perfect Vacation Destination! Plan Your Next Vacation Here! Villa de la Mer, This Seagrove Beach Condo Has it ALL... 30A! Beach, Love \& Happiness in Beautiful Seagrove! Beckoning Breeze in NatureWalk at Seagrove Beach [...]}
\smallskip

\noindent\textsc{Depth~1:} {\small\itshape ! Beckoning Breeze in NatureWalk at Seagrove Beach 30A! (Photo Courtesy of Becky Slaughter) Located in Seagrove Beach, at the southeastern end of the beautiful Emerald Coast, this charming 2 bedroom, 1 bath condo is located in a gated community. Upon arrival, the large screened-in balcony offers a spectacular 360 [...]}
